I have rewritten the portage policy using hierarchical types.  It is a
simple use of hierarchy, so it should be fairly straightforward as an
example.  Right now only the domains are hierarchical:

portage_t
\_portage_t.merge
\_portage_t.fetch
\_portage_t.sandbox

Where the fetch domain downloads packages and rsyncs portage ebuilds,
sandbox is where packages are compiled, and merge is used for merging
files out of the compile sandbox to the live filesystem.  The top level
type (portage_t) is not used except for constraining the child domains.

Since SourceForge anonymous CVS access is still down, I have attached
the portage module for reference.

